+## Multi-Provider Benchmark & Cutoff Timeout Guide
+
+Every AI provider configuration and agent definition exposes a configurable hard cutoff timeout (`timeout_ms`, `1000` to `300000` ms). At runtime, `GateWorkerRunner` enforces `cutoff_ms = min(provider.timeout_ms, agent.timeout_ms)`. When an upstream model exceeds `cutoff_ms`, the worker raises `GATE_TIMEOUT` and **fails closed**, leaving the ticket in its source state with zero hung workers.
+
+### Live Full-Stack In-Transition Benchmark Matrix (`In Progress -> Done`)
+
+Measured end-to-end against `kanban-liveqa-2` (embedded PostgreSQL 16 + `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`) using `StrictVerdictSchema` (`kb-transition-verdict/v1`) on a Positive software ticket (`KAN-1`) and a Negative impossible/unverified ticket (`KAN-2: "Build a rocket ship and serve ice cream on Saturn"`):
+
+| Runtime & Model | Cutoff (`timeout_ms`) | Positive (`KAN-1`) | Positive Latency | Negative (`KAN-2`) | Negative Latency | Operational Guidance |
+| :--- | :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- |
+| **Google Gemini** (`gemini-2.5-flash-lite`) | `20000` | `approve` (`Done`) | `3,215 ms` | `reject` (`In Progress`) | `1,594 ms` | Fastest overall cloud model with strict schema compliance and `v1beta` AI Studio routing. |
+| **OpenAI Cloud** (`gpt-4o-mini`) | `20000` | `approve` (`Done`) | `3,846 ms` | `reject` (`In Progress`) | `2,224 ms` | Fast cloud fallback with strict JSON schema adherence. |
+| **Local Ollama Supercomputer** (`gemma4:e2b`) | `25000` | `approve` (`Done`) | `19,892 ms` | `reject` (`In Progress`) | `5,213 ms` | Strong air-gapped 2B edge choice; `20000`-`25000 ms` cutoff recommended. |
+| **Local Ollama GPU/CPU** (`gemma3:4b`) | `20000` / `35000` | `timed_out` (20s) / `approve` (35s) | `20,929 ms` / `31,431 ms` | `reject` (`In Progress`) | `16,630 ms` | If VRAM is shared with another pinned model (CPU fallback), set `timeout_ms >= 35000`. |
+| **Local Ollama GPU/CPU** (`granite3.3:2b`) | `20000` | `timed_out` (fail-closed) | `20,321 ms` | `reject` (`In Progress`) | `12,691 ms` | Warm-keep or `25000 ms` cutoff avoids cold-load timeout on long prompts. |
+| **Local Ollama Reasoning** (`nemotron-3-super:latest`) | `5000` (Strict) | N/A | N/A | `GATE_TIMEOUT` (fail-closed) | `6,023 ms` | Validates hard 5s cutoff protection with clean fail-closed veto. |
+| **Local Ollama Reasoning** (`nemotron-3-super:latest`) | `45000` (Extended) | `approve` (`Done`) | `31,940 ms` | `reject` (`In Progress`) | `26,502 ms` | Heavy reasoning models (`<think>` tags stripped) should use `45000`-`60000 ms`. |
+
+### Choosing a Cutoff Timeout
+- **Fast Cloud Models (`gpt-4o-mini`, `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`):** `15000` to `20000` ms.
+- **Local 2B-4B Edge Models (`gemma4:e2b`, `gemma3:4b`, `granite3.3:2b`):** `25000` to `35000` ms (covers occasional model reload or shared VRAM).
+- **Heavy Reasoning Models (`nemotron-3-super:latest`, `deepseek-r1`):** `45000` to `60000` ms, or pair with a strict `5000`-`10000` ms cutoff on latency-sensitive columns so stuck calls fail closed immediately.
+
